#!/bin/bash
# Convergence of the div(u) = S tests that have exact solutions, with dx and dt refined
# together.  Run from this directory after building incflo2d.gnu.MPI.ex.  The Linf and L2
# norms of the errors at the final time are printed (Norm0 / Norm2).
#   inputs.divu_source_ballistic (incflo.probtype = 603), periodic: u, v, p, the density and
#     both tracers converge at second order in L2.  The max errors of the density and the
#     tracers converge more slowly, where the PPM limiter clips smooth extrema.
#   The same with two levels and a fixed fine patch over the middle of the domain: the L2
#     errors converge at second order on both levels.  Along the coarse/fine boundary the
#     error of p is first order; at the corners of the patch it stops converging and that of
#     u and v becomes first order, which limits the max errors on the fine level.  This comes
#     from the nodal projection at the coarse/fine boundary together with the viscous term:
#     with mu = 0 these errors are about 20 times smaller, and an incompressible flow with
#     the same mu (the decaying Taylor vortex) also has a first-order p there.
#   inputs.divu_source_ballistic_walls (603), no-slip walls: u, v and p converge at second
#     order; p is first order in the cells next to the walls (see the inputs file), but its
#     error there is smaller than inside at these resolutions.  The density and the tracers are
#     first order in the two cells next to the walls (see the inputs file), so their L2 errors
#     converge at between order 1.5 and 2, and the max error of the convective tracer, which is
#     largest there, at first order.
#   inputs.divu_source_mms (incflo.probtype = 604): the errors of u and v are second order.
#     The pressure is first order next to the no-slip walls (see the inputs file).
#   inputs.divu_source_temperature (incflo.probtype = 606): S = kappa (T - T_ref) is computed
#     from the temperature, and the fluid enters and leaves the domain.  u and p converge at
#     second order or faster.  The density, the tracers and the temperature converge at second
#     order in L2, and their max errors, at the peak of the warm layer, which the PPM limiter
#     clips, at order 1.6.
dt() { awk "BEGIN {printf \"%.10g\", $1/$2}"; }
for n in 32 64 128 256; do
    ./incflo2d.gnu.MPI.ex inputs.divu_source_ballistic amr.n_cell="$n $n" incflo.fixed_dt=$(dt 0.5 $n) >& out.ballistic.$n
    ./incflo2d.gnu.MPI.ex inputs.divu_source_ballistic_walls amr.n_cell="$n $n" incflo.fixed_dt=$(dt 0.5 $n) >& out.walls.$n
    ./incflo2d.gnu.MPI.ex inputs.divu_source_mms amr.n_cell="$n $n" incflo.fixed_dt=$(dt 0.5 $n) >& out.mms.$n
done
for n in 64 128 256 512; do
    ./incflo2d.gnu.MPI.ex inputs.divu_source_temperature amr.n_cell="$n $((n/8))" incflo.fixed_dt=$(dt 0.5 $n) >& out.temperature.$n
done
for n in 32 64 128; do
    ./incflo2d.gnu.MPI.ex inputs.divu_source_ballistic amr.n_cell="$n $n" incflo.fixed_dt=$(dt 0.25 $n) \
        amr.max_level=1 amr.n_error_buf=0 amr.regrid_int=-1 incflo.tag_region=true \
        incflo.tag_region_lo="0.25 0.25" incflo.tag_region_hi="0.75 0.75" >& out.ballistic_amr.$n
done
echo "Norm0 / Norm2 of the errors at the final time"
for n in 32 64 128 256; do
    echo "probtype 603, periodic, n = $n"
    grep Norm0 out.ballistic.$n | tail -6
done
for n in 32 64 128; do
    echo "probtype 603, periodic, two levels, coarse n = $n: u, v, p and the density, each on level 0"
    echo "and then on level 1; then tracer0 and tracer1 on level 0, and then on level 1"
    grep Norm0 out.ballistic_amr.$n | tail -12
done
for n in 32 64 128 256; do
    echo "probtype 603, no-slip walls, n = $n"
    grep Norm0 out.walls.$n | tail -6
done
for n in 32 64 128 256; do
    echo "probtype 604, n = $n"
    grep Norm0 out.mms.$n | tail -3
done
for n in 64 128 256 512; do
    echo "probtype 606, n = $n"
    grep Norm0 out.temperature.$n | tail -7
done
